WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.267
Unions in France

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.303
are protesting one more time

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.204
over the president's

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:05.071
pension reform,

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.006
and they say this will

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.041
likely be one of the last.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.509
They are trying to push lawmakers

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.443
to reverse course.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.178
Almost two months after the government

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.847
raise the retirement age

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.882
from 62 to 64,

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.917
March has got underway across France

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.353
and is estimated about 600,000

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:21.921
people have turned out.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.523
And these process protests

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.158
I should say which started months ago

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:25.625
if you remember

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.860
we covered them on the show.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.728
I've seen their share of violence

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:29.662
on the sideline

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.264
and some protests even stormed

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.265
the headquarters

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:35.435
of the Paris 2024 Olympic Games earlier.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.170
Melissa Bell was there

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.406
and she's standing by now for us in Paris

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:39.906
and Melissa,

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:40.640
you've been across

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.909
many of the recent protests out of Paris

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:43.743
that we've covered.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.245
How does this one did work,

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.212
this one compared

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:46.546
I mean, did

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.348
the protests achieve anything here?

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:51.351
Well, it was

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:53.987
much quieter than some of the protests

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.188
we've seen in these last few weeks.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:56.322
There was a little tear gas.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.424
There were a few scuffles,

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:58.558
but nothing on the level

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.226
of what we'd seen

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.462
last month or indeed the month before.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.564
In terms of the numbers, we had been

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.999
the authorities had been preparing

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:06.833
for 600,000.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.369
In the end, the actual figure is 281,000.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:10.770
So really under that

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.372
31,000 here in Paris.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.374
So it was much smaller protests.

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:16.376
And that, Isa, is partly

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.611
because the main union has announced

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.013
that this was likely to be the last one.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:20.580
Essentially,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.582
this reform is going to become law.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:23.183
There's very little

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:24.617
that can be done about it.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.686
But I think they will have been heartened

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.488
by the numbers

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:29.155
that have turned out

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.356
so consistently week

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:30.924
in, week out

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.392
over the course of the last six months.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.260
This began back in January.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.396
So they have sent a strong signal

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.398
that they will keep going to the streets.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.766
And I think it is for the autumn

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:40.834
and the future reforms

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.368
that Emmanuel Macron has planned

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.571
for his last four years in office

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:46.473
that they really have their eye on.

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:47.941
Of course, what this latest

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.310
series of protests has done is remind us

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.712
of just how much a part of French

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:53.580
political life

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.981
protests are in this country.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:55.582
In fact,

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.117
we got to catch up with one journalist

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.651
who essentially makes a living

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.486
from just that

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.556
Another pitched battle

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.825
between protesters and police

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.161
in the heart of Paris.

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:10.130
The images captured by a journalist

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.165
who's made this his specialty.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.468
Klimala has covered every major French

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.871
protest for the last seven years.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:21.608
His focus to document the many uprisings

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:22.742
against the government

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.077
and tell the stories

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:25.912
of the anger behind them.

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:28.014
They could not show those be used up.

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:30.450
The money is there, says one protester.

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:33.853
We just have to go and get it.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:36.322
Traveling across the city, the protesters

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.357
hush each other

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:38.358
as they get closer

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:40.627
to the Euronext Stock Exchange.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:43.930
There, they pause the

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.732
then charge

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.435
through the flares in the smoke

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.004
that engulfs the building lobby.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:52.872
The sound of anger at the French

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:54.040
president.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.010
The shocking scenes.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.179
But for Paris, nothing new.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:00.280
The protests

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.181
against the government's

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:04.350
upping of the pension age from 62 to 64

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:05.952
are just the latest round

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.854
to draw people to the streets.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:09.856
I didn't really see a party in Paris.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.691
There are protests almost every day.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:12.692
Some smaller.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:13.760
Some bigger

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.395
because in France we are used to it.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.996
As soon as something goes wrong.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.798
The French protest,

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:19.966
the hardest to cover,

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:20.700
he says,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.303
were the yellow vest protests of 20, 19

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.904
and 2020

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:25.338
avec le

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.140
police recommended for the police,

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.575
the protesters.

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:31.177
We've never seen protests that violent.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.413
Everyone was a little shaken.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:35.281
Everyone was a little changed.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:37.984
Over the years.

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:40.186
The 25 year old has been on the receiving

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:40.787
end of rubber

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.555
bullets, police batons

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:45.625
and angry tussles with protesters Being a

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:48.094
journalist is little protection, he says.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:49.896
Several times

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:50.563
I found myself

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:52.532
in the middle of the police charges.

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:54.100
They hit me with their shields,

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.201
even though they could see

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.069
I was a journalist

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:58.638
and they could have avoided me.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.807
But despite the dangers, images

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.041
like these have been earning

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:02.976
Eleanor a decent

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:05.044
living for the last seven years.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:07.380
Covering hundreds of protests, she says.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.849
In fact, the manifestos went bust.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.517
Once the demonstration is over,

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:12.619
everyone goes home

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:14.754
and life goes back to normal.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.089
You'll probably see bus stops

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.090
that have been shattered,

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.424
but life goes on

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.525
and everything is okay

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:20.360
for the Parisians

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.728
who go back out for a walk

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.796
when the protest is done.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:24.530
In a city

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.332
where the culture of protest runs

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.468
deep, it's just another day

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:30.903
and another cleanup of the streets of

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:31.838
the French capital.

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:36.276
Is even as this

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:38.177
latest round of protest

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.179
now seems to be petering out.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.148
What we look ahead to is a September

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:43.416
where essentially the French will start

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:44.817
working longer incrementally.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.919
The government has got its way, Isa.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:48.288
And this is all for us

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:49.222
and Paris is for you.

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:50.156
Thanks very much, Melissa.

